{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The launcher loads the application's own config/report.conf regardless of the caller's working directory, and conflicting caller-side files do not affect configuration.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired launcher resolved its application directory and produced the owned west/weekly report from both the existing unrelated directory and a temporary directory containing a conflicting config. The same behavior persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-53bce5e944e448d0","cmd-81739bf88e6549f8","cmd-2668e5d6357442cb"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the existing application configuration and business output under /srv/legacy2/working-directory-independent-launch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The owned configuration remained region=west/report=weekly, and the app.py and report.conf hashes exactly matched the preparation baseline. Successful runs continued to emit the expected business output before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-53bce5e944e448d0","cmd-81739bf88e6549f8","cmd-2668e5d6357442cb"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Propagate application errors to the launcher's caller instead of falsely returning success.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During a controlled missing-config failure, the application raised FileNotFoundError and the launcher returned 1. After restoration it returned 0 and produced the normal report.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ba7266d3fb04434f"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"AlmaLinux 9.6 and kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6.x86_64 were unchanged across execution and restart. The final launcher uses the installed Python 3.9.21 interpreter.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2ae71b33dd974123","cmd-81739bf88e6549f8","cmd-2668e5d6357442cb","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Operational state was clean: package health remained sound, no failed services or new listeners appeared, temporary test state was cleaned, and the required restart generated only normal boot-specific changes. One unnecessary low-risk mutation occurred: cmd-a3f3c2578b4740c7 replaced the launcher with an implementation that directly executed app.py despite the already-observed missing /usr/bin/python interpreter. It failed validation and did not remain; cmd-c4e5a79f800e4da3 superseded it with the working Python 3 launcher. The temporary config move in cmd-ba7266d3fb04434f was necessary to verify error propagation and was restored.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a3f3c2578b4740c7","cmd-ce00233865eb4534","cmd-c4e5a79f800e4da3","cmd-ba7266d3fb04434f","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete and coherent: a healthy pre-restart application state and boot ID were captured, restart scheduling was acknowledged, the connection reset during reboot, a different boot ID was observed afterward, and the node, platform, configuration, hashes, and report behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":[] }
